(Bug #83: `not` now sits between `and` and the comparison level, so every
 operand slot of `and`/`or` reads it the same way. Before the fix only a
 leading `not` was even reachable, and it bound to the primary next to it.)

To calm with a number called temperature.
  Return a boolean, not temperature is greater than 10.

a number called heat is 3.
a number called limit is 6.
a boolean called door_open is false.
a boolean called alarm_armed is true.

(Left and right of `and`, and left of `or`.)
If heat is 3 and not limit is 5 then,
    Print "right of and: fires".
Otherwise,
    Print "right of and: silent".

If not heat is 4 and limit is 6 then,
    Print "left of and: fires".
Otherwise,
    Print "left of and: silent".

If not heat is 4 or limit is 99 then,
    Print "left of or: fires".
Otherwise,
    Print "left of or: silent".

(Two `not`s cancel, because the inner one takes the comparison and the
 outer one takes the inner.)
If not not heat is limit then,
    Print "double: fires".
Otherwise,
    Print "double: silent".

(The `but if` guard and the guarded `print` take a condition too.)
If heat is 99 then,
    Print "unreachable".
But if not heat is limit then,
    Print "but if: fires".
Otherwise,
    Print "but if: silent".

Print "guarded print: default", but if not heat is limit print "guarded print: fires".

(A plural subject list is one comparison, so `not` takes all of it.)
If not door_open, alarm_armed, and door_open are true then,
    Print "plural subjects: fires".
Otherwise,
    Print "plural subjects: silent".

(A returned condition, and a loop condition.)
If calm of 3 is true then,
    Print "returned condition: fires".
Otherwise,
    Print "returned condition: silent".

a number called tick is 3.
While not tick is greater than 5,
    Print "loop tick {tick}",
    increment tick.
